<title>USA: Glaxo completes sale of N.C. drug facility.</title>
<headline>Glaxo completes sale of N.C. drug facility.</headline>
<dateline>RESEARCH TRIANGLE PARK, N.C. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome Plc's U.S. unit said Thursday that it has completed the sale of its pharmaceutical plant in Greenville, N.C. to a subsidiary unit of Catalytica Inc.</p>
<p>The company said that it sold the facility, where about 1,100 people work, for $247 million, cash. Glaxo also received warrants of Catalytica, common shares of its subsidiary unit, and a share of operating profits from the facility.</p>
</text>
